N:drama-skills
D:[drama-skills] Install, route, and operate zenstory-ai/drama-skills, the MIT-licensed creator-first suite of ten independent Agent Skills for Chinese short dramas and motion comics. Routes novel triage, adaptation development, episode writing, visual assets, image prompts, storyboards, video prompts, independent review, local Dashboard operations, and confirm-gated image/video/TTS/music production while preserving five human-readable episode documents. Python 3.9+; normal work is stdlib-only and keyless; external production may spend real money.
G:drama-skills zenstory-ai short-drama motion-comic Chinese-drama novel-adaptation screenwriting visual-assets image-prompts storyboard video-prompts creator-first dashboard production-review python

U[8]:
  Install, pin, update, inspect, or troubleshoot the upstream ten-skill suite
  Initialize, continue, inspect, package, or open the local Dashboard for a drama project
  Triage a long novel before deciding whether to adapt it
  Develop a source or idea into direction, a creative brief, story engine, and episode map
  Write or revise an episode and derive its visual identity and continuity
  Produce copy-ready image prompts, shot plans, frozen keyframes, or video prompts
  Independently review story, assets, prompts, continuity, or existing media
  Prepare optional image, video, TTS, or music jobs behind exact user confirmation

S[7]{n,step,details}:
  1,Pick one mode,install-maintain or route-create or project-ops or produce or troubleshoot; never blend paid production into writing
  2,Pin and inspect,record the local tag/commit; do not mix v0.5 and v0.6 outputs; load only the selected upstream skill and references
  3,Route one owner,short-drama for project ops; otherwise novel-analyze develop write assets image-prompts storyboard video-prompts produce or review
  4,Preserve ownership,剧本.md 视觉设定.md 分镜.md 图片提示词.md 视频提示词.md are creator truth; validators and JSON indexes are derived
  5,Use lifecycle tools correctly,init makes config and empty directories; selftests are maintenance-only; Dashboard stays loopback-only
  6,Gate production,prepare exact preview then explicit fingerprint confirmation then one run; never reprepare/confirm/run a pending attempt; changes and failed retries need fresh confirmation
  7,Verify and report,mode version owner inputs files checks unresolved decisions and exact production state

R[10]:
  Start from the stage whose real input exists; do not fabricate a ceremonial upstream pipeline
  short-drama is a router and project operator, not an installation gate for the other nine skills
  Only the stage owner writes its source document; review reports findings instead of silently rewriting it
  Do not auto-add review, packaging, or production to a scoped creative request
  Prefer a pinned release over symlinking a moving main branch into an agent skill root
  v0.6 creator-first is a breaking change from v0.5; keep existing v0.5 projects pinned
  Upstream snapshot b7846a0 separates IMG prompt-entry IDs from REF input-reference slots; recheck other versions
  Stage selftests run only for install, upgrade, or troubleshooting; normal creation stays file-first
  Adapter config and credentials live outside the project and secret values never appear in output
  Generic programmable video routes to video-production; webtoon panels to webtoon-harness; OpenStory codebase work to openstory

E[6]{type,command}:
  Install this routing skill,npx skills add https://github.com/akillness/jeo-skills --skill drama-skills
  Read-only suite check,bash .agent-skills/drama-skills/scripts/drama-skills.sh doctor /path/to/drama-skills
  Print stage routes,bash .agent-skills/drama-skills/scripts/drama-skills.sh routes
  Read-only project check,bash .agent-skills/drama-skills/scripts/drama-skills.sh project /path/to/project
  Initialize upstream project,python3 <suite>/skills/short-drama/scripts/project_tool.py init ./my-drama --title "Example drama"
  Inspect upstream project,python3 <suite>/skills/short-drama/scripts/project_tool.py status ./my-drama
